      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This paper describes the central findings and discusses the clinical implications of the Helsinki Heart Study. This was a controlled primary prevention trial to test the hypothesis that using gemfibrozil to lower the concentrations of serum low density lipoprotein (LDL) and very low density lipoprotein (VLDL) and to raise that of high density lipoprotein (HDL) protects subjects against coronary heart disease."},
